---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// DRAFT — the owner approves legal wording before this publishes
// (ROSETTA_ACCOUNTS.md A8 owner prerequisites). Every processor named below was
// read out of the actual code, not assumed: Firebase Auth (app + site),
// Anthropic (`MO_MODEL` in mo-backend/app/config.py), Stripe (app/billing/),
// Modal (modal_app.py), Apple (IAP, A7). If a processor is added, this list is
// part of shipping it.
const updated = 'July 2026';
const contact = 'support@rosetta.fun';
---

<Base title="Privacy · Rosetta" description="What Rosetta collects, why, and who else sees it.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="faint">Last updated: {updated}</p>

  <p>
    Rosetta is a guitar app. It needs very little about you, and this page is the complete list of what it
    does need. We don't sell your data, we don't run ads, and we don't track you across other websites.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your account.</strong> An email address, and a user ID we generate. If you sign in with Apple,
      Google, X or Facebook, we receive whatever that provider tells us — typically an email address and a
      display name. If you use Sign in with Apple's private relay, we only ever see the relay address.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What you ask Mo for.</strong> The descriptions you type when you ask Mo to make a song, and the
      songs it makes back. We keep these to run the feature, to stop abuse, and to see where Mo gets it wrong.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Usage counts.</strong> How many songs you've made, your remaining allowance and credits, and
      timestamps for them. This is how allowances and purchases work at all.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Purchases.</strong> If you buy something, we store which purchase it was and a transaction ID
      from Stripe or Apple. <strong>We never see or store your card details.</strong>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    <strong>What we don't collect:</strong> no contacts, no location, no microphone recordings, no advertising
    identifiers, and no analytics that follow you to other sites. The songs you write yourself in the app stay
    on your device unless you choose to share them.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else processes it</h2>
  <p>We use a small number of companies to run the service. They only handle your data to do that job.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google (Firebase Authentication)</strong> — sign-in and account identity.</li>
    <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> — the AI model behind Mo. Your song description is sent there to generate a song.</li>
    <li><strong>Modal</strong> — hosting for our servers and database.</li>
    <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — payments made on this website, including card handling.</li>
    <li><strong>Apple</strong> — purchases made inside the iOS app, and Sign in with Apple.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where your data goes</h2>
  <p>
    These providers are based in the United States, and your information is stored and processed there. If you
    are in the UK, EU or another region with data-transfer rules, using Rosetta means your data is transferred
    to the United States under the relevant standard contractual clauses or equivalent safeguards our
    providers maintain.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we're allowed to hold it</h2>
  <p>
    We process your account and usage data to provide the service you asked for (contract), and a minimum
    amount to keep the service from being abused (legitimate interests). We keep purchase records as long as
    tax and accounting rules require.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete your account at any time — in the app under Profile, or on <a href="/account">this website</a>.
    Deleting removes your sign-in, your usage history, your balance and any remaining credits from our
    servers. It is permanent and we can't restore it. Backups roll off within 30 days. Records we're legally
    required to keep for accounting purposes are retained for that purpose only.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Deletion is
    self-service (above); for anything else, email <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a> and we'll
    respond within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Rosetta isn't directed at children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their data. If you believe a
    child has created an account, email us and we'll delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no advertising or analytics cookies. Signing in stores your session in your browser so
    you stay signed in — that's it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy in a way that matters, we'll say so in the app and on this page before it takes
    effect.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a></p>
</Base>
